.TH WREX-VLAN 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-vlan \- vlan layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIvlan\fR \fB--vlan\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIvlan\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
IEEE 802.1Q VLAN tag: 4\-byte header (TCI: pcp 3 bits + dei 1 bit + vid 12 bits, then the encapsulated ethertype). Stacks on eth (or another vlan for QinQ/802.1ad double tagging; craft emits 0x8100, 0x88a8 is dissect\-only). type drives the chain like eth.type: 0x0800 \-> ipv4, 0x0806 \-> arp, 0x86dd \-> ipv6, 0x8100/0x88a8 \-> vlan, else synthesized `unknown`.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 15; stacks on eth, vlan (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --vlan-pcp).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-pcp=\fIINT\fR\fR
priority code point (0\-7, 3 bits) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-dei=\fIINT\fR\fR
drop eligible indicator (0/1, 1 bit) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-vid=\fIINT\fR\fR
VLAN identifier (0\-4095, 12 bits; 0 = priority tag) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-vlan\-type=\fIINT\fR\fR
encapsulated ethertype (autofill: derived from next layer) Type u16. Default: 0.

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex fields vlan

